berately\n\nEnabling single-dollar means two currency amounts in one paragraph collide. Measured, not assumed:\n\n- `\"It costs $12.50 today.\"` → fine (lone `$`, no closer)\n- `\"Between $5 and $10 per unit.\"` → **`inlineMath(\"5 and \")`**\n- `` `echo $HOME` `` → fine (code span)\n- `\\$5` → fine (escape works)\n\nThis is exactly why Streamdown ships the flag off. Every chat UI that renders LaTeX enables it anyway and accepts the collision; the alternative is a hand-rolled \"does this look TeX-shaped\" heuristic, which is more complexity for a rarer case. `\\$` is the opt-out.\n\nThe two halves are independent — if you'd rather ship only the single-dollar fix, the `normalizeMathDelimiters` half can be dropped on its own.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vitest --project unit` — 25 pass, including 15 new `normalizeMathDelimiters` cases (rewrites, code-span/fence exclusion, streaming-partial no-ops).\n- `vitest --project storybook message.stories` — 6 pass, including the new `MathDelimiters` story, which asserts 4 rendered `.katex` nodes plus the `\\$20` and code-span literals surviving. This is the assertion that actually exercises `MessageResponse` → `Streamdown` → plugins, rather than a hand-built unified pipeline.\n- Full storybook suite: 265/267. The 2 failures are in `button-group.stories.tsx` (\"you either have no stories or none are selected\" — the preview iframe not loading under full-suite load); it passes 9/9 in isolation and shares no code with this change.\n- `lint` + `typecheck` clean on `@workspace/ui` and `storybook`.\n\n## Not covered\n\n4-space-indented code blocks are not excluded from the delimiter rewrite (fenced blocks and inline code are). Model output effectively never uses that form.\nEOF\ngh pr create --base master --head worktree/fix-latex-in-messages --title \"fix(ui): render inline and escaped-delimiter LaTeX in messages\" --body-file $S/pr-body.md",
